V\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The FCC's I2C transactions to address 0x40 would receive no acknowledge, so the servo PWM outputs would not be driven as designed.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The schematic is broadly consistent with the specification, but LED1 is drawn directly across the 5 V rail with no series resistor, unlike every other indicator LED. The PCA9685 address strap (A0 high, giving 0x41) also conflicts with the specified 0x40.\"\n}",
